<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Operation Gomorrah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1943">1943</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Operation Gomorrah was a series of British and American air raids on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamburg">Hamburg</a> in late July and early August 1943. On the night of 27–28 July, hot, dry weather and concentrated bombing created a firestorm that devastated eastern districts of the city. Around 35,000 people were killed and hundreds of thousands fled, making it one of the deadliest air attacks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-gomorrah.jpg" alt="Operation Gomorrah" width="320" height="265" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dowd J (Fg Off), Royal Air Force official photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Air_Force_Bomber_Command,_1942-1945._CL3400.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
